-LABEL-TARGETS.csv links each published label to its review, source table, outcome, time point and contrast, with quoted binding evidence where stated and an explicit inference otherwise. The assessment prompt targets the labelled result rather than automatically the trial primary outcome, with the definition, printed result and locator from the trial report. Among the 102 included trials, 33 targets match an explicitly stated result, 11 match one of several covered outcomes, and 32 match an inferred result; 7 partly match, 9 differ and 10 have unknown binding. These categories are retained rather than treating all targets as exact matches. Twelve published label sets (60 domain labels) cover every outcome taken from a trial; another 10 label sets (50 domain labels) have no identified result, and seven more label sets (35 domain labels) jointly cover pain and disability; thus 29 sets (145 domain labels) do not isolate a single result (19 broad and 10 unknown). Binding was inferred rather than explicitly stated for 62 label sets, overlapping these categories. Source: benchmark README-FOR-ALI.md, LABEL-TARGETS.csv and per-review BINDING.md; label-target-summary.csv recomputes matching categories.
+The benchmark label-target documentation links each published label to its review, source table, outcome, time point and contrast, with quoted binding evidence where stated and an explicit inference otherwise. The assessment prompt targets the labelled result rather than automatically the trial primary outcome, with the definition, printed result and locator from the trial report. Among the 102 included trials, 33 targets match an explicitly stated result, 11 match one of several covered outcomes, and 32 match an inferred result; 7 partly match, 9 differ and 10 have unknown binding. These categories are retained rather than treating all targets as exact matches. Twelve published label sets (60 domain labels) cover every outcome taken from a trial; another 10 label sets (50 domain labels) have no identified result, and seven more label sets (35 domain labels) jointly cover pain and disability; thus 29 sets (145 domain labels) do not isolate a single result (19 broad and 10 unknown). Binding was inferred rather than explicitly stated for 62 label sets, overlapping these categories. The benchmark documentation and per-review binding evidence support these categories (eTable 11).
